        {
          "text": "The tail is **N8633A**, and the 142-minute departure delay propagates through **five more legs on 2026-01-03** before the overnight at HOU kills it. Minimum turn is 35 minutes at every station involved (SFO, PHX, LGB, LAS, DAL \u2014 each has \u2265139 observed turns, and the 5th-percentile ground time is 35 min at all of them; carrier-wide p05 is also 35).\n\nProjection, walking the rotation forward from a 18:17Z off / 20:27Z on at SFO:\n\n| Leg | Sched dep (UTC) | Projected dep | Dep delay | Turn buffer eaten |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2026-01-03\\|WN\\|4106\\|SFO\\|PHX\\|1055 | 18:55 | 21:02 | **+127** | 50 sched \u2212 35 min = 15 absorbed |\n| 2026-01-03\\|WN\\|172\\|PHX\\|LGB\\|1440 | 21:40 | 23:37 | **+117** | 45 \u2212 35 = 10 absorbed |\n| 2026-01-03\\|WN\\|65\\|LGB\\|LAS\\|1545 | 23:45 | 01:37 (1/4) | **+112** | 40 \u2212 35 = 5 absorbed |\n| 2026-01-03\\|WN\\|65\\|LAS\\|DAL\\|1735 | 01:35 (1/4) | 03:22 | **+107** | 40 \u2212 35 = 5 absorbed |\n| 2026-01-03\\|WN\\|65\\|DAL\\|HOU\\|2255 | 04:55 (1/4) | 06:37 | **+102** | 40 \u2212 35 = 5 absorbed |\n| 2026-01-04\\|WN\\|2999\\|HOU\\|STL\\|0500 | 11:00 (1/4) | 11:00 \u2014 on time | 0 | 295 min of ground, absorbs the remaining 102 |\n\nTotal pushed downstream: **565 minutes of departure delay across five legs**, ending at HOU. The day's turns only absorb 40 minutes in total (15 at SFO, 10 at PHX, 5 each at LGB, LAS, DAL) \u2014 the schedule is built at or barely above minimum turn from SFO onward, so essentially nothing recovers in-day. The real absorber is the 295-minute overnight sit at HOU, which swallows the remaining 102 minutes; WN2999 the next morning departs clean.\n\nWhat actually happened on this tail matches and slightly exceeds the projection: those same five legs went out +144, +135, +140, +144, +155, with the delay-cause file attributing 133, 128, 124, 116 and 114 minutes respectively to late_aircraft \u2014 i.e. the cascade is the dominant cause on every one of them, with only 1\u201325 minutes of fresh carrier delay added per leg. WN2999 HOU\u2013STL then departed +3 and arrived \u22128, confirming the break point. Note the original 141 minutes of arrival delay on WN3851 itself was attributed entirely to NAS, not to an inbound aircraft.",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
